What are Aluminum Plates?
Aluminum plates are flat-rolled aluminum products with thicknesses starting from 0.250 inches (approximately 6.35 mm) and above, distinguishing them from thinner sheets and foils. These plates deliver an exceptional strength-to-weight ratio, remarkable corrosion resistance, and good machinability, making them indispensable for demanding structural applications across numerous industries. Their versatility enables use in everything from aircraft fuselages and automotive chassis to marine structures and architectural cladding, offering durability and performance advantages over competing materials. The material's inherent recyclability also aligns with global sustainability initiatives, enhancing its appeal in environmentally conscious markets.
